    "explanation": "To both parties: the $4.00 no-show cancellation fee charged on trip TRP-00412 is not chargeable. I order it refunded in full to the rider. No driver compensation is payable and no referral is made.\n\nWhy the fee fails. POL-NS-01 makes a no-show fee chargeable only if all four of its conditions hold. The first two do: the trip record carries the driver's 'arrived' event at 12:45:20, and the GPS trace (EV-GPS-00412) places him inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius at that exact moment, with 21 consecutive qualifying fixes and no gaps, so the marker is genuine — POL-NS-05 does not fire and no false-arrival entry is made against the driver. But condition (c) requires him to hold position inside the geofence for the free waiting period in force, and the trip record's own platform_policy states that period as 300 seconds; the 180-second default in fee_schedule does not apply, because the resolution rule reads platform_policy first. The driver's qualifying dwell is 200 seconds (EV-GPS-00412, single run 12:45:20–12:48:40, 21 fixes). That is 100 seconds short, and condition (d) fails with it, since he terminated the trip at 12:48:40 before the required dwell had elapsed. POL-NS-06 therefore refunds the cancellation-fee line in full. Its accumulation route cannot rescue the shortfall: the trace shows only one in-geofence interval, and the traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00412-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT), so limb (i) is unavailable and that absence can be turned to neither party's advantage.\n\nOn the rider's presence. EV-GPS-00412's rider track shows her stationary 68–76 m from the pin throughout the window, i.e. inside the 100 m STANDARD presence radius, so the driver's account of an absent rider is not made out. It does not matter either way: POL-NS-06 refunds a wait shortfall whether or not the rider was present and whether or not she replied. The driver's statement that he arrived on time and messaged with no reply cannot extend the clock or make 200 seconds equal 300, and POL-NS-04's exoneration route (which needs a locating message from the rider) simply is never reached, because she sent none.\n\nOn the profiles. POL-GEN-01 makes the driver's rating, lifetime trips and the rider's prior_no_show_flags context only; neither side's appeal to history carries any weight here. The POL-NS-07 anti-farming check does not trip (1 termination against 120 completed trips in 30 days), the parties have no disputes between them in the trailing 90 days, and rider no_show_disputes_30d is 1, so no POL-NS-09 trigger is engaged and the case is decided rather than escalated. The fare line reconciles exactly with the fee in force for this trip ($4.00 net), so POL-NS-08(d) is clean; payment_status is CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd is 0.00, and the $4.00 returned is that line. The monetary effect ($4.00) is within the $8.00 automatic execution threshold. This is a provisional ruling made without human review; either party may appeal once, within 30 days, through the platform's help channel. Two claims were flagged for merely mentioning context-only profile fields — both sides correctly treated those fields as unusable — and no claim was discarded."
